	(text "DESIGN NOTES (S32K3xx data sheet; S32K3 Hardware Design Guidelines Rev E2; Node60 compute page)\nGATE-MCU-01 PASSED 2026-10-28: all 257 balls and every planned function checked against NXP IOMUX (Nov 2025), IBIS and\n  BSDL (257BGA); signed off by the user. Re-run it if the pin plan changes. The pin table above each unit is the plan.\nSupplies: VDD_HV_A = VDD_HV_B = VREFH = 3V3_MAIN, V15 = 1V5_CORE (U303), V11/V25 internal (decoupling only).\n  NTC dividers are ratiometric to 3V3_MAIN = VREFH. Check the S32K3 supply ramp-rate limits against the LMQ66430\n  soft start (HDG 2.10.1) during bring-up.\nClock: 16 MHz crystal on FXOSC (DEC-015), core and peripherals via PLL; CMU monitors FXOSC. Unused GPIOs\n  unconnected (disabled), as NXP HDG Rev E2 Table 33 requires. RESET_B pulled up to VDD_HV_A (4.7k on p3), as Table 33 requires.\nWatchdog: internal SWT, hard-locked after start-up (DEC-005). Clock monitor CMU -> reset.\nRESET_B (PTA5) on RESET_L: TPS3702 window supervisor (p3) wired-OR, PHY RESET_N, debug header pin 10.\nFlash IS25LP032D-JNLA3 on LPSPI2, mode 0 or 3, own CS with 10k pull-up so it is deselected through reset;\n  WP and HOLD pulled up (single-IO SPI). Powered from switched 3V3_MAIN; log flush before PHY sleep (DEC-007).\nDebug: Cortex 10-pin (project default). Pin 7 is the key, pin 8 unused. SWDIO 10k up, SWCLK 10k down.\nDefault states: all port pins are disabled inputs out of reset; LPSPI4 PCS0 and LPSPI2 PCS0 are held high by\n  the switch's internal pull-up and R4xx respectively; FLT and IRQ lines idle high via their pull-ups.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
